WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:00.834
The president

00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:01.501
of the University

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.535
of Pennsylvania, Liz

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:03.870
McGill, has resigned.

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.472
And we've just gotten word

00:00:05.472 --> 00:00:06.873
that the chair of the University

00:00:06.873 --> 00:00:07.507
of Pennsylvania's

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:08.775
Board of Trustees, Scott

00:00:08.775 --> 00:00:10.744
Bock, has also resigned

00:00:10.744 --> 00:00:11.945
effective immediately.

00:00:11.945 --> 00:00:13.513
The new Penn controversy

00:00:13.513 --> 00:00:15.015
began spiraling earlier

00:00:15.015 --> 00:00:16.449
this week after McGill's

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:17.984
testimony before Congress

00:00:17.984 --> 00:00:20.020
about anti-Semitism on campus

00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:23.256
specifically calling

00:00:23.256 --> 00:00:25.158
for the genocide of Jews.

00:00:25.158 --> 00:00:26.593
Does that constitute

00:00:26.593 --> 00:00:29.295
bullying or harassment?

00:00:29.763 --> 00:00:31.131
If it is directed

00:00:31.131 --> 00:00:32.265
and severe or pervasive,

00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:33.533
it is harassment.

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:35.502
So the answer is yes.

00:00:35.502 --> 00:00:37.470
It is a context dependent decision.

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:38.371
Congresswoman, it's

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:40.106
a context dependent decision.

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:41.041
That's your testimony.

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:41.341
Today.

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:43.143
Calling for the genocide of Jews

00:00:43.143 --> 00:00:46.813
is depending upon the context

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:48.148
that was Tuesday.

00:00:48.148 --> 00:00:49.149
And this was the clean up

00:00:49.149 --> 00:00:51.384
attempt by Liz McGill on Wednesday.

00:00:53.153 --> 00:00:55.155
In that moment, I was focused

00:00:55.155 --> 00:00:57.924
on our university's longstanding policies

00:00:58.425 --> 00:01:00.293
aligned with the U.S. Constitution,

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:01.861
which say

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:04.264
that speech alone is not punishable.

00:01:05.231 --> 00:01:07.300
These policies need to be clarified

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:09.736
and evaluated

00:01:12.072 --> 00:01:13.940
That obviously was not enough.

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:15.975
And of course, she has now stepped down.

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:17.310
So has the

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:18.711
chair of the board of trustees

00:01:18.711 --> 00:01:20.180
at the University of Pennsylvania.

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:22.382
And we have team coverage on all of this

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:24.451
union's polls and of all, Matt Egan.

00:01:24.451 --> 00:01:25.819
Paula, let me start with you.

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:27.420
What's the latest? What can you tell us?

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:29.222
The developments have been swift moving

00:01:29.222 --> 00:01:29.722
here, Jim,

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:30.924
with Liz McGill tonight

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:32.492
announcing that she will be

00:01:32.492 --> 00:01:33.793
stepping down amid

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:36.062
that growing chorus of calls

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:38.364
for asking for her resignation.

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:39.632
In light of that testimony,

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:41.434
that she offered in Washington

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:41.968
just this

00:01:41.968 --> 00:01:43.536
past Tuesday in a statement

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:45.705
released by the university.

00:01:45.705 --> 00:01:48.141
We have learned that McGill is expected

00:01:48.141 --> 00:01:51.711
to remain tenured as faculty at Penn

00:01:52.011 --> 00:01:52.879
Carey Law

00:01:52.879 --> 00:01:54.581
and that she has also agreed to stay

00:01:54.581 --> 00:01:56.883
on at least until the interim

00:01:57.817 --> 00:01:58.485
president

00:01:58.485 --> 00:01:59.586
can potentially be

00:01:59.586 --> 00:02:01.521
be appointed for some context here.

00:02:01.521 --> 00:02:04.224
McGill has been under growing scrutiny

00:02:04.224 --> 00:02:04.557
for her

00:02:04.557 --> 00:02:06.993
handling of anti-Semitism on campus.

00:02:07.327 --> 00:02:08.461
And that testimony

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:09.662
that was offered on Tuesday

00:02:09.662 --> 00:02:10.663
was really

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:11.931
the last straw here,

00:02:11.931 --> 00:02:13.967
mainly referring to that,

00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:14.601
or at least her

00:02:14.601 --> 00:02:17.470
her inability to just equivocal to say

00:02:18.004 --> 00:02:21.808
that any mention of genocide of Jewish

00:02:21.808 --> 00:02:22.942
people would

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:25.245
be against the code of conduct

00:02:25.245 --> 00:02:27.046
at the university.

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:28.348
We should also mention that, you know,

00:02:28.348 --> 00:02:29.849
we heard from other university

00:02:29.849 --> 00:02:30.783
officials tonight,

00:02:30.783 --> 00:02:31.885
including

00:02:31.918 --> 00:02:32.952
one that we'll talk about here

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:33.620
in a few moments,

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:34.220
but basically trying

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:35.722
to paint a clearer picture

00:02:35.722 --> 00:02:37.490
of what he believed

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:38.358
played out

00:02:38.358 --> 00:02:39.159
on Tuesday,

00:02:39.159 --> 00:02:40.593
saying that McGill was,

00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:42.295
quote, overprepared,

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:43.997
that she was overly lawyered

00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:45.431
and essentially provided

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:48.635
a legalistic answer to a moral question.

00:02:48.635 --> 00:02:49.769
So what you have now

00:02:49.769 --> 00:02:52.539
is coming from the now former chair

00:02:52.906 --> 00:02:54.841
of you, Penn's board of trustees,

00:02:54.841 --> 00:02:56.342
trying to explain

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:56.976
what was an

00:02:56.976 --> 00:02:58.711
absolutely disastrous testimony

00:02:58.711 --> 00:02:59.846
that played out on Tuesday.

00:03:01.581 --> 00:03:02.782
And let me go to Matt Eagan.

00:03:02.782 --> 00:03:04.150
Matt, I know you've been reporting

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:05.485
on the school

00:03:05.485 --> 00:03:07.187
being under tremendous pressure

00:03:07.187 --> 00:03:07.921
from donors

00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:09.289
the donor community

00:03:09.289 --> 00:03:11.791
has been outraged over these comments.

00:03:11.958 --> 00:03:15.428
Take us behind the scenes on that

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:17.897
Jim, of remarkable developments

00:03:17.897 --> 00:03:19.632
this evening at one of the nation's

00:03:19.632 --> 00:03:21.334
most prestigious schools.

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:23.102
First, the board chair, Scott

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:24.370
Bok, sent out a letter

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:25.004
saying that

00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:26.806
the president, Liz McGill, is out.

00:03:26.806 --> 00:03:27.840
Then Scott Bok

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.008
sent out a statement saying

00:03:29.008 --> 00:03:31.010
he's out to now.

00:03:31.010 --> 00:03:33.546
Make no mistake, both of these leaders

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:35.848
were under pressure for months,

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:37.283
as Polo just said.

00:03:37.283 --> 00:03:38.284
And again, it was over

00:03:38.284 --> 00:03:40.086
issues of anti-Semitism on campus.

00:03:40.086 --> 00:03:42.222
But Tuesday's hearing,

00:03:42.222 --> 00:03:43.389
which can only be described

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:44.824
as disastrous,

00:03:44.824 --> 00:03:47.193
really was the final straw.

00:03:47.227 --> 00:03:49.996
I mean, that hearing lasted for hours,

00:03:49.996 --> 00:03:51.631
but it really just came down

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:53.967
to just a precious few minutes where

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:57.270
the leaders of Penn and Harvard and MIT,

00:03:57.604 --> 00:03:58.571
they struggled. Right?

00:03:58.571 --> 00:04:00.106
I mean, they struggled to answer

00:04:00.106 --> 00:04:00.707
a question

00:04:00.707 --> 00:04:02.609
that many people would think

00:04:02.609 --> 00:04:04.510
would be easy to answer. Right.

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:06.879
Does calls for genocide of Jews,

00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:09.048
does that break the school's route rules?

00:04:09.549 --> 00:04:11.517
And the leaders, including McGill.

00:04:11.517 --> 00:04:13.586
They think they fumbled that response.

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:13.753
Right.

00:04:13.753 --> 00:04:16.055
They did give kind of a legal answer.

00:04:16.055 --> 00:04:18.524
And that moment went viral

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:20.760
on the Internet. It just exploded.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:22.462
The backlash was so intense.

00:04:22.462 --> 00:04:23.296
We heard from

00:04:23.296 --> 00:04:25.031
the Walton Board of Advisors,

00:04:25.031 --> 00:04:26.699
which is basically a who's

00:04:26.699 --> 00:04:28.134
who of business leaders.

00:04:28.134 --> 00:04:29.402
They called for an immediate

00:04:29.402 --> 00:04:31.671
leadership change at the school.

00:04:31.671 --> 00:04:34.340
More than 70 members of Congress, a

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:35.942
bipartisan group

00:04:35.942 --> 00:04:37.410
calling for McGill to resign.

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:37.710
It's it's

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.445
hard to get 70 members of Congress

00:04:39.445 --> 00:04:40.313
to agree on much,

00:04:40.313 --> 00:04:41.648
but they agreed on that.

00:04:41.648 --> 00:04:42.815
You also had the former U.S.

00:04:42.815 --> 00:04:43.816
ambassador, John

00:04:43.816 --> 00:04:44.784
Huntsman, telling me

00:04:44.784 --> 00:04:46.552
that it wasn't even debatable

00:04:46.552 --> 00:04:47.887
whether or not McGill should leave.

00:04:47.887 --> 00:04:50.356
And you also had one mega-donor

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:54.127
threatening to cancel a $100 million

00:04:54.127 --> 00:04:57.196
gift if a change wasn't me.

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:59.198
Now, Scott Bok was effusive

00:04:59.198 --> 00:05:00.700
in his praise of Liz McGill,

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:02.669
calling her a very good person,

00:05:02.669 --> 00:05:03.169
saying that she's

00:05:03.169 --> 00:05:05.038
not in the slightest bit anti-Semitic.

00:05:05.038 --> 00:05:05.905
I want to read you a

00:05:05.905 --> 00:05:08.741
one line from boxed statement.

00:05:08.941 --> 00:05:09.976
He said,

00:05:10.009 --> 00:05:11.010
talking about the hearing,

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:12.779
overprepared and over lawyer

00:05:12.779 --> 00:05:15.148
given the hostile forum in high stakes,

00:05:15.381 --> 00:05:16.182
she provided

00:05:16.182 --> 00:05:17.817
a legal is the answer

00:05:17.817 --> 00:05:19.152
to a moral question.

00:05:19.152 --> 00:05:20.887
And that was wrong.

00:05:20.887 --> 00:05:23.823
It made for a dreadful 32nd soundbite

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:25.291
in what was more

00:05:25.291 --> 00:05:27.527
than 5 hours of testimony.

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:29.329
So, Jim, there you have it.

00:05:29.329 --> 00:05:31.597
You have both Liz McGill and Scott Buck

00:05:31.831 --> 00:05:34.667
stepping down after that disastrous

00:05:34.667 --> 00:05:36.169
hearing on Tuesday.

00:05:36.169 --> 00:05:38.037
Yeah, just a devastating afternoon

00:05:38.037 --> 00:05:39.372
for the University of Pennsylvania.

00:05:39.372 --> 00:05:39.872
All right.

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:41.941
Polo Sandoval and Matt Egan,

00:05:41.941 --> 00:05:42.942
thanks to both of you.

00:05:42.942 --> 00:05:44.544
I want to bring in Alex Project.

00:05:44.544 --> 00:05:45.845
He's a professor

00:05:45.845 --> 00:05:48.247
with the UPenn School of Medicine.

00:05:48.247 --> 00:05:50.950
Professor, what's your response tonight?

00:05:52.485 --> 00:05:54.787
Well, frankly,

00:05:54.787 --> 00:05:56.089
I can't say I'm happy

00:05:56.089 --> 00:05:57.457
because it's hard to be happy

00:05:57.457 --> 00:05:58.591
about all the things

00:05:58.591 --> 00:05:59.092
that have been

00:05:59.092 --> 00:06:00.593
happening at the university.

00:06:00.593 --> 00:06:03.463
But I do believe that Louis McGill

00:06:03.463 --> 00:06:04.697
could not have continued

00:06:04.697 --> 00:06:06.966
being the president, given

00:06:06.966 --> 00:06:08.134
the number of

00:06:08.134 --> 00:06:09.435
I would see mistakes

00:06:09.435 --> 00:06:11.838
that she and people who

00:06:11.838 --> 00:06:13.339
I guess may be lawyers tear up

00:06:13.339 --> 00:06:15.041
and prepared to provide.

00:06:15.041 --> 00:06:16.342
I think she lost the trust

00:06:16.342 --> 00:06:18.878
of the community, of faculty,

00:06:19.212 --> 00:06:20.613
donors, students.

00:06:20.613 --> 00:06:21.114
Of course,

00:06:21.114 --> 00:06:22.815
people have very complex opinions

00:06:22.815 --> 00:06:25.518
about the Israeli-Palestinian conflict.

00:06:25.518 --> 00:06:26.719
But this is about something

00:06:26.719 --> 00:06:28.388
completely different.

00:06:29.122 --> 00:06:30.723
And I mean,

00:06:30.723 --> 00:06:33.092
the chair of the board Scott Bok,

00:06:33.926 --> 00:06:34.861
tried to describe it

00:06:34.861 --> 00:06:36.763
as just a 32nd soundbite

00:06:36.763 --> 00:06:37.663
that did not go

00:06:37.663 --> 00:06:40.032
well for President McGill.

00:06:40.032 --> 00:06:42.368
But we talked to a Penn student

00:06:42.368 --> 00:06:43.703
in the last hour

00:06:43.703 --> 00:06:44.604
who has described

00:06:44.604 --> 00:06:47.507
a pretty hostile atmosphere on campus

00:06:47.507 --> 00:06:48.841
and that this has been

00:06:48.841 --> 00:06:51.043
building for some time.

00:06:51.043 --> 00:06:52.245
How would you describe things?

00:06:53.813 --> 00:06:55.848
Well, I definitely think

00:06:55.848 --> 00:06:57.750
that the sound bites during

00:06:57.750 --> 00:07:00.119
the hearings did not help, but

00:07:00.119 --> 00:07:01.020
that Miss McGill

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:02.121
could have helped herself

00:07:02.121 --> 00:07:05.825
by issuing a once lawyered up apology or

00:07:05.958 --> 00:07:07.760
explanation of what happened

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:09.128
during that hearing.

00:07:09.128 --> 00:07:10.563
And unfortunately,

00:07:10.563 --> 00:07:12.698
that, too, was kind of canned.

00:07:13.132 --> 00:07:15.401
And I don't think anybody who heard

00:07:15.902 --> 00:07:19.071
that post sort of post-hoc

00:07:19.305 --> 00:07:20.740
description felt

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:22.642
that it was at all sincere.

00:07:22.642 --> 00:07:24.143
So I don't think it is

00:07:24.143 --> 00:07:24.911
fair to say

00:07:24.911 --> 00:07:26.112
it's just an unfortunate

00:07:26.112 --> 00:07:27.480
sound like we will said things

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:28.748
we did not mean,

00:07:28.748 --> 00:07:30.016
but given an opportunity

00:07:30.016 --> 00:07:31.517
to clarify the situation.

00:07:31.517 --> 00:07:34.387
She she did not do that.

00:07:34.387 --> 00:07:35.388
And how do you think this news

00:07:35.388 --> 00:07:36.189
is going to be received

00:07:36.189 --> 00:07:38.024
by students, by the faculty?

00:07:38.024 --> 00:07:39.091
What do you think

00:07:40.293 --> 00:07:41.160
Well,

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:43.963
I think people have different opinions.

00:07:43.963 --> 00:07:45.965
And maybe that's the important

00:07:45.965 --> 00:07:50.136
bit is that I understand that you know,

00:07:50.236 --> 00:07:51.370
the lack of desire

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:53.272
to unequivocally condemn

00:07:53.272 --> 00:07:54.407
calls for genocide

00:07:54.407 --> 00:07:55.274
is sort of coached

00:07:55.274 --> 00:07:57.343
within the framework of free speech.

00:07:57.343 --> 00:07:59.912
But unfortunately, and many people

00:07:59.912 --> 00:08:00.413
have written

00:08:00.413 --> 00:08:02.048
and spoken about this, it's

00:08:02.048 --> 00:08:03.850
hard to cast universities you like.

00:08:03.850 --> 00:08:05.051
You can

00:08:05.251 --> 00:08:07.620
sort of very much pro-free speech.

00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:09.222
Speech tends to be limited

00:08:09.222 --> 00:08:10.890
in many different respects.

00:08:10.890 --> 00:08:12.091
So I am actually

00:08:12.091 --> 00:08:13.259
a proponent of free speech.

00:08:13.259 --> 00:08:15.061
So I think people are probably going

00:08:15.061 --> 00:08:16.863
to have very different opinions

00:08:16.863 --> 00:08:19.065
depending on where they stand politically

00:08:19.332 --> 00:08:20.199
and how they feel

00:08:20.199 --> 00:08:22.268
about the Israeli-Palestinian

00:08:22.268 --> 00:08:23.436
conflict, etc.

00:08:23.436 --> 00:08:24.337
And that's a good thing.

00:08:24.337 --> 00:08:25.938
People shouldn't be having debates.

00:08:25.938 --> 00:08:27.974
They shouldn't cross over into violence.

00:08:27.974 --> 00:08:30.076
They shouldn't cross over into hate

00:08:30.076 --> 00:08:31.711
speech, etc.

00:08:31.711 --> 00:08:34.080
But within the sort of norms of

00:08:34.680 --> 00:08:35.515
human behavior,

00:08:35.515 --> 00:08:37.016
I think people should differ

00:08:37.016 --> 00:08:39.218
on their opinions and have conversations.

00:08:39.218 --> 00:08:39.952
And why do you think

00:08:39.952 --> 00:08:42.021
we saw the chair of the board,

00:08:42.021 --> 00:08:44.490
Scott Bok, resign in addition to that to

00:08:44.657 --> 00:08:45.725
the university's president?

00:08:47.126 --> 00:08:47.593
You know,

00:08:47.593 --> 00:08:48.261
I'm not really

00:08:48.261 --> 00:08:48.594
privy,

00:08:48.594 --> 00:08:50.763
of course, to any of these discussions.

00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:53.332
I suspect that

00:08:53.633 --> 00:08:55.535
maybe there is a realization

00:08:55.535 --> 00:08:57.770
that they've waited a bit too long,

00:08:58.304 --> 00:09:00.540
that maybe

00:09:00.873 --> 00:09:03.209
with the number of again, unfortunate

00:09:03.242 --> 00:09:06.045
and in my opinion, incorrect moves

00:09:06.779 --> 00:09:09.482
she could not have really governed

00:09:09.482 --> 00:09:11.117
and sort of corrected the course.

00:09:11.117 --> 00:09:14.921
So I don't know if the idea to

00:09:14.954 --> 00:09:15.955
keep loose.

00:09:15.955 --> 00:09:17.423
McGill longer

00:09:17.423 --> 00:09:18.024
than she probably

00:09:18.024 --> 00:09:19.525
should have stayed came from Buck

00:09:19.525 --> 00:09:21.594
and maybe that is why

00:09:21.594 --> 00:09:23.763
he decided to step down but

00:09:23.763 --> 00:09:25.231
I would be just guessing. I don't know.

